1
00:00:06,548 --> 00:00:13,192
Two weeks. I said I could do it in two weeks, and I did it.

2
00:00:13,192 --> 00:00:19,735
The pictures you've taken are fabulous, Richard.

3
00:00:19,735 --> 00:00:28,135
Mr. Carlson will love them.

4
00:00:28,135 --> 00:00:28,802
Monday morning.

5
00:00:28,802 --> 00:02:52,722
I'm going to show him the photos on Monday morning.

6
00:02:52,722 --> 00:02:53,460
I can't wait!

7
00:02:53,460 --> 00:02:57,929
I'm very proud of you. You really did a beautiful job.

8
00:02:57,929 --> 00:03:09,212
I know he will love the new photographs for your book.

9
00:03:09,212 --> 00:03:17,139
Yeah. I really did do a good job, didn't I?

10
00:03:17,139 --> 00:03:20,963
Hey, you know? There's still some film left on this roll,

11
00:03:20,963 --> 00:03:28,161
and there's one person I haven't photographed in a long time.

12
00:03:28,161 --> 00:03:28,457
Who?

13
00:03:28,457 --> 00:03:28,726
You.

14
00:03:28,726 --> 00:03:31,435
Richard! I haven't brushed my hair. Richard,

15
00:03:31,435 --> 00:03:34,185
You look great!

16
00:03:34,185 --> 00:03:38,391
It's not fair, Richard. I'm not even ready.

17
00:03:38,391 --> 00:04:13,127
Oh, that's wonderful! That's wonderful!

18
00:04:13,127 --> 00:04:14,407
Thanks.

19
00:04:14,407 --> 00:04:16,105
Fabulous!

20
00:04:16,105 --> 00:04:19,083
Thanks.

21
00:04:19,083 --> 00:04:20,083
Terrific!

22
00:04:20,083 --> 00:04:22,060
Thanks.

23
00:04:22,060 --> 00:04:25,038
They get better and better.

24
00:04:25,038 --> 00:04:28,016
Thanks a lot.

25
00:04:28,016 --> 00:04:29,648
This is sensational!

26
00:04:29,648 --> 00:04:30,994
Yeah. Thanks.

27
00:04:30,994 --> 00:04:36,950
What a job! Good work, Richard!

28
00:04:36,950 --> 00:04:39,390
I'm so glad you like them so much.

29
00:04:39,390 --> 00:04:42,906
Like them? They represent your best work.

30
00:04:42,906 --> 00:04:44,406
Really?

31
00:04:44,406 --> 00:04:45,884
Absolutely.

32
00:04:45,884 --> 00:04:52,832
Well ... what do you think? Do I have my book?

33
00:04:52,832 --> 00:05:00,774
You do. You do. There's a book here.

34
00:05:00,774 --> 00:05:01,814
I'll have a contract

35
00:05:01,814 --> 00:05:04,249
and an advance payment waiting for you

36
00:05:04,249 --> 00:05:04,687
first thing in the morning.

37
00:05:04,687 --> 00:05:04,887
Thank you.

38
00:05:04,687 --> 00:05:07,440
And while you're here,

39
00:05:07,440 --> 00:05:09,708
I would like to introduce you to your editor.

40
00:05:09,708 --> 00:05:12,686
And I want you to meet the people in the art department.

41
00:05:12,686 --> 00:05:15,103
I'll set up an appointment with the marketing people.

42
00:05:15,103 --> 00:05:16,151
When do you think we'll be through?

43
00:05:16,151 --> 00:05:19,048
In about half an hour. Why?

44
00:05:19,048 --> 00:05:22,048
I can't wait to tell Marilyn!
